      "section": "What I’m reading —",
      "category": "article",
      "title": "The Art of Spirited Away",
      "creator": "Hayao Miyazaki",
      "note": "_Spirited Away_—as mentioned in [my chat with Adam Savage](https://el2.convertkit-mail2.com/c/5qu8lqg33u7h5g97m/r7a8hoh39g2nmk/aHR0cHM6Ly90aW0uYmxvZy8yMDE5LzA0LzMwL2FkYW0tc2F2YWdlLz91dG1fc291cmNlPWNvbnZlcnRraXQmdXRtX21lZGl1bT1jb252ZXJ0a2l0JnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj01YmY=)—is my favorite movie of all time. This book is awe-inspiring and shows the depth of world-creation that makes Miyazaki a legend.",
